# bench/w5/scale/forkaudit.allow -- the REVIEWED call tasks inside forking defs (make fork-audit; forkaudit.py --check).
#
# Format: `caller_regex -> callee_regex | reason` (fullmatch on the normalised names of the emitted C: lowercase,
# without the FID_/src_ prefix, without the _K/_C/_J<n> segment suffix; a template instance `_<n>` is matched by
# `(_\d+)?`). A forking def is a def with a parallel let. A call to a non-flat fork-free callee from inside it
# compiles to a TASK (`return term_tsk(..)`) that the scheduler's grow pass does not run (DESIGN.md 16.10); it is
# harmless in exactly three positions, and every entry names its position:
#   leaf    the unit of work of the fork: the arm of the match that does NOT fork (the tree's leaf). The grow pass
#           skips the task on purpose, the drain runs it on a thread of its own.
#   root    the call sits in a sequential prelude or before a ROOT fork called from the sequential program
#           (the main thread is never in a grow turn). None is needed today: the roots (Lst.pmap, Sort.pm,
#           Csv.v2.lanes, ...) are not forking defs, so they do not appear.
#   join    the continuation after the fork (`_J<n>`; filtered out by the tool, no entry needed).
# Anything else (a call in a branch argument, work before the parallel let in a recursive forking def) is a
# violation: build the work tree in a sequential prelude and fork by match only.
#
# The gate sees (def, callee) pairs, not sites: when you touch a forking def, read its diff.

cexec_cx_p1 -> cexec_cx_wrapf | leaf: FTL arm = CX.p1.leaf (the leaf frame wrapped for the evaluator); no fork follows in that arm
cexec_cx_p1 -> cexec_cx_lframe | leaf: FTL arm = CX.p1.leaf; T5.5's compiled predicate: the PF5 / PBad arms hand the leaf frame back as a one-leaf CFrame (CX.p1.f5); no fork follows in that arm
cexec_cx_p1 -> eval_eval_f5_go | leaf: FTL arm = CX.p1.leaf, PF5 arm (T5.5: the F5 plan compiled once for the walk, the passes run per leaf); no fork follows in that arm
cexec_cx_p3 -> cexec_cx_splitn | leaf: FTL arm = CX.p3.leaf (T5.5's one-walk filter: the leaf splits its columns after the predicate's, then F5 passes and compaction); no fork follows in that arm
cexec_cx_p2 -> cexec_cx_lframe | leaf: FTL / FTB / mismatch arms hand the compacted leaf frame back as a one-leaf CFrame; no fork follows
cexec_cx_w2 -> cexec_cx_wrapf | leaf: FTL arm = CX.w2.leaf (the leaf frame wrapped for the evaluator); no fork follows in that arm
chunks_c[wfs]_rechunk_go -> chunks_c[wfs]_flatten | leaf: the `fits` arm builds ONE leaf by one flatten of the subtree; only the not-fits arm forks
chunks_lst_pmap_t(_\d+)? -> chunks_cnamed_to | leaf: f(p, x) of Lst.pmap.t at an LTL leaf (the column job, the unit of work); no fork follows
csv_csv_v2_bfork -> csv_csv_v2_kone | leaf: QKL arm builds ONE column (concatenation + dictionary merge), the unit of work of the column fork
csv_csv_v2_cfork -> csv_csv_v2_ch_kone | leaf: QKL arm builds ONE column's chunk trees (W6.6: merge + leaf cut), the unit of work of the column fork
sort_sort_pm_t(_\d+)? -> fmt_fmt_d_job | leaf: f(p, x) of Sort.pm.t at a PTL leaf (one describe column's statistics); no fork follows
